%% Sequence diagrams do not support classDef. Planned participants carry " (NEW)" in the label and sit in the dashed-label box.
sequenceDiagram
  participant A1 as Browser user
  participant C14 as UI script
  participant C3 as SessionAuthMiddleware
  participant C4 as SessionStore
  participant C6 as AuthController
  participant C18 as DemoUser (config)
  participant C19 as UserSession
  participant C7 as InvoicesController
  participant C5 as RequireRole filter
  participant C8 as ApprovalsController
  participant C10 as ApprovalService
  participant C15 as Invoice
  participant C11 as IInvoiceRepository
  box rgba(150,150,150,0.15) Planned, not built (NEW). Solid participants above exist today.
  participant C21 as Azure SQL repository (NEW)
  participant C22 as Azure SQL database (NEW)
  participant C25 as Outbox worker (NEW)
  participant C27 as Concurrency cap and circuit breaker (NEW)
  participant C26 as PayEx client (NEW)
  participant A2 as PayEx (NEW)
  participant C29 as Alerts (NEW)
  end
  A1->>C14: sign in
  C14->>C6: S1: POST /api/auth/login (middleware skips this path)
  C6->>C18: S2: username and password matched to configured users, 401 if none
  C6->>C19: S3: new UserSession(username, role), role copied from DemoUser
  C6->>C4: S4: session created
  C14->>C3: S5: POST /api/invoices/id/submit with Bearer token
  C3->>C4: S6: token lookup, 401 if no session
  C3->>C7: S7: any signed-in role may submit
  Note over C3,C7: Framework routing between middleware and controller omitted
  C7->>C10: S8: Submit(id) via Handle
  C10->>C11: S9: invoice must be Draft else 409, set PendingApproval, Update
  C14->>C3: S10: POST /api/approvals/id/approve or reject
  C3->>C4: S11: token validation, 401 if invalid
  C3->>C5: S12: role must be Approver or Admin else 403
  C5->>C8: S13: allowed
  C8->>C10: S14: Approve(id, username) or Reject(id, username, reason)
  C10->>C10: S15: blank reject reason throws, mapped to 400
  C10->>C11: S16: invoice must be PendingApproval else 409, 404 if missing
  C10->>C15: S17: set Status Approved or Rejected, DecidedBy, DecidedAt, DecisionNote
  C10->>C11: S18: Update(invoice)
  C11->>C21: S21: Update is served by the Azure SQL repository (NEW)
  Note over C21,C22: One SQL transaction on approval
  C21->>C22: S22: update invoice status
  C21->>C22: S23: INSERT append-only audit event
  C21->>C22: S24: INSERT outbox row, state Pending, unique per invoice
  C21->>C22: S25: COMMIT
  C8-->>C14: S20: 200 with invoice JSON
  Note over C8,C25: Approval returns here. Submission to PayEx happens later in the worker.
  C25->>C22: S26: claim Pending row, set Submitting, lease longer than client timeout plus margin
  C25->>C27: S27: call passes the concurrency cap and circuit breaker
  C25->>C26: S28: submit invoice
  C26->>A2: S29: send with invoice Id as idempotency key, client timeout set in configuration to at least 30 s
  alt Success
    A2-->>C26: S30: returns a reference
    C25->>C22: S31: row Submitting to Submitted
  else PayEx timeout
    A2--xC26: S32: no response within the timeout, outcome unknown
    C25->>C22: S33: row Submitting to InDoubt (not Failed), with reason code
    C25->>C29: S34: InDoubt count and PayEx timeout rate feed alerts
    Note over C25,C29: A person resolves the row by lookup or by a retry with the same key. Never a bulk reset to Pending.
  end
